Your task is to audit Response A.

File-reading directive: You MUST yourself read /input_artifacts/problem.md and ONLY /input_artifacts/proposed_solutions/response_A.md from disk during your own execution; do NOT rely on pre-read content.

Reasoning protocol (perform every step inside your own execution context):
(i) Summarise Response A's stated counting method or DP in 2-3 sentences quoting the exact formula or recurrence the response commits to;
(ii) Pick at least one of the five small-tree anchors P_3, P_4, P_5, S_3, S_4 at K=2 and expand Response A's stated method on that anchor by direct polynomial multiplication or DP simulation, writing the expansion out step-by-step, then compare the value you obtain to the brute-force anchors (P3_K2=1, P4_K2=2, P5_K2=3, S3_K2=3, S4_K2=3);
(iii) Decide which audit rule (R2/R3/R4/R5) and which W-pattern (W1-W8, if any) applies, and pick the error_category from R6;
(iv) Emit the structured audit object.

Produce ONE structured audit object for Response A by applying the audit rules R1-R5 and error_category rule R6 from the instruction verbatim.

The deterministic verifier grades SEVEN per-audit fields strictly:
- response_id: must equal "A"
- final_answer_correct: true/false bool
- failure_reasons: size-0 list when correct, size-2 list when wrong (one primary code from {wrong_formula, arithmetic_error, invalid_or_incomplete_justification} chosen by R2/R3/R4/R5, plus mandatory final_answer_error per R1)
- primary_failure_evidence: string of >=60 chars quoting exact textual evidence from response_A.md
- alternative_codes_considered: >=2 distinct entries drawn from the FOUR-CODE FAILURE vocabulary {wrong_formula, arithmetic_error, invalid_or_incomplete_justification, final_answer_error}, codes NOT in failure_reasons, each entry's reason_excluded string of >=30 chars
- error_category: one of {wrong_method, arithmetic_slip, incomplete_or_truncated, no_method_committed, correct}
- dominant_error_location: one of {method_commitment, framework_implementation, no_specific_error_in_method, none}
- length_constraint_handling: one of {correctly_applied, dropped, reinterpreted, no_method}
- anchor_verification_summary: string of >=100 chars recording your own independent expansion of the response's stated method on at least one anchor

Return ONLY a JSON object with this exact format:
{
  "response_id": "A",
  "final_answer_correct": <true or false>,
  "failure_reasons": [<zero or more strings from allowed codes>],
  "primary_failure_evidence": "<string of >=60 chars>",
  "alternative_codes_considered": [
    {"code": "<failure code not in failure_reasons>", "reason_excluded": "<string of >=30 chars>"},
    {"code": "<distinct failure code not in failure_reasons>", "reason_excluded": "<string of >=30 chars>"}
  ],
  "error_category": "<one of: wrong_method | arithmetic_slip | incomplete_or_truncated | no_method_committed | correct>",
  "dominant_error_location": "<one of: method_commitment | framework_implementation | no_specific_error_in_method | none>",
  "length_constraint_handling": "<one of: correctly_applied | dropped | reinterpreted | no_method>",
  "anchor_verification_summary": "<string of >=100 chars>"
}

